<title>SOUTH KOREA: SEOULBANK says capital reserves rise.</title>
<headline>SEOULBANK says capital reserves rise.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's SEOULBANK said on Thursday its capital reserves increased by 418.8 billion won after a re-evaulation of its real estate holdings.</p>
<p>A bank official said the bank's net worth also increased to 2.02 trillion won as a result of the assset re-evaluation.</p>
<p>Further details were not given.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
